-- title:
--   Assumption 4.2 — the $(\gamma,r)$-gap ensuring condition
-- statement:
--   **Assumption 4.2.** Let $r>0$ and $\gamma\in(0,1]$. For every $t\ge1$, whenever
--
--   $$
--   \max_{k\in[m]} d(y^{t,0},y^{t,k})\le r ,
--   $$
--
--   there is an orthogonal decomposition $\{P'_{t,k}\}_{k\in[m]}$ of $T_{y^{t,0}}M$ such that for all $k\in[m]$, $P_{t,k}$ and $P'_{t,k}$ have the same rank and
--
--   $$
--   \|P'_{t,k}-P_{t,k}\|_{y^{t,0}}\le\gamma ,
--   $$
--
--   the induced operator norm on $T_{y^{t,0}}M$. A selection rule with this property is called **$(\gamma,r)$-gap ensuring**.
--
--   The condition asks that, as long as an inner loop stays within distance $r$ of its start, the transported projections stay uniformly close to an orthogonal decomposition. It replaces the exact coordinate decomposition of Euclidean block coordinate descent.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $P'_{t,k}$ is the orthogonal projection onto the $k$-th subspace of an orthogonal decomposition; its rank is the dimension of that subspace, and the rank of $P_{t,k}$ is the dimension of its range. The paper states the condition for every sequence generated by Algorithm 1 with the rule; here it is imposed along a given run.
-- source:
--   Gutman & Ho-Nguyen, Coordinate Descent Without Coordinates, arXiv:1912.10627v3, Assumption 4.2, p.11

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_RiemSetting
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_IsOrthDecomp
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_TSDRun
import Definitions.Def_TSDRiem_TSDRun_Ptk

namespace TSDRiem

/-- Assumption 4.2, the `(γ, r)`-gap ensuring condition, along a run: `r > 0`, `γ ∈ (0, 1]`, and
for every `t ≥ 1`, whenever `max_{k∈[m]} d(y^{t,0}, y^{t,k}) ≤ r`, there exists an orthogonal
decomposition `{P′_{t,k}}_{k∈[m]}` of `T_{y^{t,0}}M` such that for all `k ∈ [m]`, `P_{t,k}` and
`P′_{t,k}` have the same rank and `‖P′_{t,k} − P_{t,k}‖_{y^{t,0}} ≤ γ` (the induced operator norm
on `T_{y^{t,0}}M`).

Gutman & Ho-Nguyen, Coordinate Descent Without Coordinates, arXiv:1912.10627v3, Assumption 4.2,
p.11.

Formalization Note: `P′_{t,k}` is `(K k).starProjection` for an orthogonal decomposition `K`
(`IsOrthDecomp`); its rank is `finrank (K k)`, and the rank of `P_{t,k}` is the dimension of its
range. The operator norm is that of `T_{y^{t,0}}M →L[ℝ] T_{y^{t,0}}M`. Lean's `k : Fin m` is the
paper's `k + 1`, so `R.y t k.succ` ranges over `y^{t,1}, …, y^{t,m}`. The paper states the
assumption for every sequence generated by Algorithm 1 with the rule `P`; here it is imposed along
the given run (generalization). -/
def TSDRun.GapEnsuring {M : Type*} [MetricSpace M] {T : M → Type*}
    [∀ x, NormedAddCommGroup (T x)] [∀ x, InnerProductSpace ℝ (T x)]
    [∀ x, FiniteDimensional ℝ (T x)] {S : RiemSetting M T} {grad : (x : M) → T x} {m : ℕ}
    (R : TSDRun S grad m) (γ r : ℝ) : Prop :=
  0 < r ∧ 0 < γ ∧ γ ≤ 1 ∧ ∀ t, 1 ≤ t → (∀ k : Fin m, dist (R.y t 0) (R.y t k.succ) ≤ r) →
    ∃ K : Fin m → Submodule ℝ (T (R.y t 0)), IsOrthDecomp K ∧ ∀ k,
      Module.finrank ℝ (K k) =
          Module.finrank ℝ (LinearMap.range (R.Ptk t k : T (R.y t 0) →ₗ[ℝ] T (R.y t 0))) ∧
        ‖(K k).starProjection - R.Ptk t k‖ ≤ γ

end TSDRiem


